# .agents: Antigravity on top of the Claude Code setup

{% if use_claude_code %}
Claude Code and Antigravity work in this project side by side. The instructions stay in one place,
`.claude/` and `CLAUDE.md`; this folder only points Antigravity at them. Change behaviour there,
not here.
{% else %}
The instructions live in `.claude/` and `CLAUDE.md`, in Claude Code's layout, and this folder
only points Antigravity at them. Change behaviour there, not here.
{% endif %}

| Claude Code | Antigravity | How |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `CLAUDE.md` | `rules/project.md` | always-on rule that inlines `CLAUDE.md` |
{% if custom_repo_name %}
| `src/{{ custom_repo_name }}/CLAUDE.md` | `rules/addons-conventions.md` | glob rule over the addons checkout and `.worktrees/` |
{% endif %}
| Claude-only tools, kb, safety | `rules/antigravity.md` | always-on rule, Antigravity-only text |
| `.claude/skills/` | `skills.json` | registers the folder; the Claude Code mods are excluded |
| `.claude/agents/*.md` | `agents/*.md` | frontmatter for Antigravity, body reads the Claude file |
| hooks in `.claude/settings.json` | `hooks.json` + `hooks/claude_hook.py` | runs the same scripts, translating payloads |
{% if use_entire %}
{% if custom_repo_name %}
| `entire` + `.claude/hooks/entire-fanout.sh` | `hooks.json` + `hooks/entire-fanout.sh` | `entire hooks antigravity` in root + fan-out to `src/{{ custom_repo_name }}` |
{% else %}
| `entire` + `.claude/hooks/entire-fanout.sh` | `hooks.json` + `hooks/entire-fanout.sh` | `entire hooks antigravity` in root + fan-out to nested repos under `src/` |
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
| `permissions.deny` (Read) | `hooks/claude_hook.py` | denied in PreToolUse |
{% if status_mcp == 'teams' %}
| claude.ai connectors | `plugins/` | `plugins/teams-mcp/` (`okolovmark/teams-mcp`) + project-local MCP plugins |
{% else %}
| claude.ai connectors | `plugins/` | project-local MCP plugins |
{% endif %}
| workspace customizations UI | `plugins/workspace-inspector/` | `Overview → Plugins → Workspace Customizations` sidecar panel (mirrored to `~/.gemini/config/plugins/` by `hooks/claude_hook.py`) |
{% if use_pipeline and custom_repo_name %}
| `pipeline-gates` mod | `plugins/pipeline-gates/` + `hooks/claude_hook.py` | `Pipeline` sidecar panel (`sidecar://pipeline-gates/panel/`) + PreToolUse/PostToolUse gate enforcement |
{% endif %}
{% if custom_repo_name %}
| `odoo-env-band` mod | `plugins/odoo-env/` | `Odoo Env & Worktrees` sidecar panel (`sidecar://odoo-env/panel/`) for PostgreSQL, git checkouts, and worktree envs |
{% endif %}

`hooks/claude_hook.py` answers a PreToolUse call it has no objection to with an empty stdout, as
entire's own Antigravity hook does: `{}` reads as an empty decision and denies the call, and
`{"decision": "allow"}` would approve it past Antigravity's permission settings.

{% if use_claude_code %}
Not ported, Claude Code only: the status line, the Claude Code mods (`rules/antigravity.md` says
what to do instead), the claude.ai connectors, `settings.local.json` permissions and auto-mode
rules (Antigravity keeps its permissions in Settings), and agent memory.
{% else %}
`.claude/settings.json` is kept because it wires the hooks the adapter runs. The Claude Code-only
parts (the mods, the markdown memory seed) are generated with `use_claude_code` only;
`rules/antigravity.md` says what to do where a skill names one of them.
{% endif %}
